--- doc/manual/R-admin.texi	(revision 90763)
+++ doc/manual/R-admin.texi	(working copy)
@@ -3845,6 +3845,12 @@
 builds of @I{OpenBLAS} and @I{BLIS}, and perhaps others@footnote{for
 example, Intel @I{MKL} not packaged by Fedora.}.  This can be controlled
 from a running @R{} session by package @CRANpkg{flexiblas}.
+On Windows, setting @code{USE_FLEXIBLAS = YES} in
+@file{src/gnuwin32/MkRules.local}, with the @I{FlexiBLAS} bundle unpacked
+as @file{@var{R_HOME}/FlexiBLAS}, makes @file{Rblas.dll} and
+@file{Rlapack.dll} forward to @I{FlexiBLAS}; its configuration is in
+@file{@var{R_HOME}/etc/flexiblasrc}, and the environment variable
+@env{FLEXIBLAS} selects the backend.
 
